  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Entry pass and 1v1 on the low post",
  "description": "A wing passer with the ball, a post player on the block and a post defender. The post player works deep, sits into the defender low and wide, and shows a target hand on the open side. The passer reads the defence: a bounce pass past the defender when they play behind or on the side, a lob over the top when they front and the space behind is open.\n\nOn the catch the post player feels where the defender is and plays 1v1: a drop step to the open side and a two-foot power finish, or a shot fake and step through (up-and-under). If a help defender comes, the post kicks it out to the wing, who has relocated to a new shooting spot. Switch roles after three attempts.\n\nStart without live defence so the entry and footwork are solid. Progression: add a help defender from the other side who can double when they like. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Post: low and wide, seat and forearm into the defender – catch with two hands and chin the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Entry: pass to the target hand, away from the defender. Bounce when they play behind, lob when they front."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Feel the defender before you turn: drop step to the side they are not on."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Passer: relocate after the entry so you are an open kick-out if help comes."
    }
  ],
